  "decision": "Accept v579 as a bounded, rights-tracked technical character fallback over v570: all five independently morphed MakeHuman/MPFB bodies now carry weighted Hair02 geometry with variant-specific imported materials, item-level CC BY 4.0 provenance, attribution, and automated skeletal-mesh material-slot validation. The terminal head fallback now uses the authored parent-to-head shaft rather than MakeHuman's unsuitable local +Z axis, eliminating the approximately 90-degree backward head regression seen in v576. Measured hair crown clearance informs a 1.22 production helmet shell and [3, 0, 1] cm center offset. D4 contact, wrap, pin, recovery, indentation, wetness, crew command, weight action, and rescue authority remain unchanged. Reject the frame for photoreal, marketing, store, press, and human approval because facial anatomy and silhouettes, clumpy fallback hair/helmet integration, hands and poses, PFD and clothing, raft, boulder, broad water, lighting, shoreline, spray, and terrain remain visibly synthetic or unfinished."
